{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"web_search_instructions":"Vercel API PATCH project disable SSO deployment protection ssoProtection deploymentType endpoint"},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"web_search_instructions":"Vercel API PATCH project disable SSO deployment protection ssoProtection deploymentType endpoint"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research Report: Vercel API PATCH project disable SSO deployment protection ssoProtection deploymentType endpoint\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nDisabling Single Sign-On (SSO) protection for deployments in Vercel can be achieved by updating the project's settings via the Vercel API. This involves sending a PATCH request to the project's endpoint with the `ssoProtection` field set to `null`. Additionally, managing deployment protection bypasses for automation purposes can be handled through specific API endpoints.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n- **Finding 1:** To disable SSO protection for a Vercel project, send a PATCH request to the `/v9/projects/{idOrName}` endpoint with the `ssoProtection` field set to `null`. ([openapi-explorer.vercel.app](https://openapi-explorer.vercel.app/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 2:** The `ssoProtection` field is part of the project's settings and can be modified using the Vercel API to enable or disable SSO protection as needed. ([openapi-explorer.vercel.app](https://openapi-explorer.vercel.app/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 3:** For automation purposes, Vercel provides a Protection Bypass feature that allows automated tools to bypass deployment protection mechanisms by using a generated secret. ([examples.vercel.com](https://examples.vercel.com/docs/deployment-protection/methods-to-bypass-deployment-protection/protection-bypass-automation?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 4:** The Protection Bypass for Automation feature is available on all Vercel plans and can be managed through the project's settings or via the API. ([examples.vercel.com](https://examples.vercel.com/docs/deployment-protection/methods-to-bypass-deployment-protection/protection-bypass-automation?utm_source=openai))\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Source Analysis\n\n### Source 1: Vercel API Reference\n\n- **URL:** https://openapi-explorer.vercel.app/\n\n- **Domain:** openapi-explorer.vercel.app\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official API documentation)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Vercel API Reference provides detailed information on updating project settings, including the `ssoProtection` field. By sending a PATCH request to the `/v9/projects/{idOrName}` endpoint with the `ssoProtection` field set to `null`, users can disable SSO protection for a specific project. The documentation outlines the required parameters and expected responses for this operation.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Endpoint: `/v9/projects/{idOrName}`\n\n- Method: PATCH\n\n- Field to update: `ssoProtection`\n\n- Value to disable: `null`\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Update the fields of a project using either its `name` or `id`.\"\n\n> \"The `ssoProtection` field can be set to `null` to disable SSO protection.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 2: Protection Bypass for Automation\n\n- **URL:** https://examples.vercel.com/docs/deployment-protection/methods-to-bypass-deployment-protection/protection-bypass-automation\n\n- **Domain:** examples.vercel.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** September 24, 2025\n\n- **Source Type:** Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official Vercel documentation)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThis documentation explains the Protection Bypass for Automation feature, which allows automated tools to bypass deployment protection mechanisms such as SSO, password protection, and trusted IPs. Users can generate multiple bypass secrets for a project, each with an optional note for identification. These secrets can be used in HTTP headers or query parameters to bypass protection during automated processes.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Feature: Protection Bypass for Automation\n\n- Available on: All Vercel plans\n\n- Usage: Set HTTP header `x-vercel-protection-bypass` with the generated secret\n\n- Optional header: `x-vercel-set-bypass-cookie` to maintain bypass state\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"The Protection Bypass for Automation feature lets you bypass Vercel Deployment Protection for automated tooling.\"\n\n> \"Each generated secret can be used to bypass deployment protection on all deployments in a project until it is revoked.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 3: Vercel API: Re-fetching shareable link for protected deployments\n\n- **URL:** https://community.vercel.com/t/vercel-api-re-fetching-shareable-link-for-protected-deployments/32379\n\n- **Domain:** community.vercel.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** January 29, 2026\n\n- **Source Type:** Community Discussion\n\n- **Credibility:** Medium (Community-sourced information)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThis community discussion addresses the challenge of retrieving a previously generated shareable link for protected deployments. The absence of a GET operation in the API for this purpose is noted, and workarounds such as storing the response or revoking and recreating the protection bypass are suggested. The discussion highlights the need for better API ergonomics in managing protected deployment links.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Issue: No GET operation to retrieve existing shareable links\n\n- Workaround 1: Store the response of the initial PATCH request\n\n- Workaround 2: Revoke and recreate the protection bypass\n\n- API endpoints involved: `PATCH /aliases/{id}/protection-bypass`, `DELETE /v1/deployments/{id}/protection-bypass`\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"I’m looking for information on how to fetch a protected deployment’s previously minted shareable URL.\"\n\n> \"The most reliable approach "}],"_meta":{"openai/widgetSessionId":"b9ca9a23-e54f-4155-9091-9720c7a2c186"},"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
